        "node_id": "PR_kwDOBOx6Lc5BIgNn",
        "number": 13,
        "title": "Fix a couple corner cases when asking for > size of ring",
        "user": {
          "login": "ypisetsky",
          "id": 287854,
          "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjI4Nzg1NA==",
          "gravatar_id": "",
          "url": "https://api.github.com/users/ypisetsky",
          "type": "User",
          "site_admin": false
        },
        "labels": [],
        "state": "closed",
        "locked": false,
        "assignee": null,
        "assignees": [],
        "milestone": null,
        "comments": 0,
        "created_at": "2022-10-19T18:48:23Z",
        "updated_at": "2022-10-19T22:00:48Z",
        "closed_at": "2022-10-19T21:21:37Z",
        "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
        "active_lock_reason": null,
        "draft": false,
        "pull_request": {
          "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/discord/ex_hash_ring/pulls/13",
          "merged_at": "2022-10-19T21:21:37Z"
        },
        "body": "Somewhat counterintuitively, the number of entries in the ring is not the upper bound on how many entries `find_nodes` and friends can find. Overrides are not required to be in the ring (but are allowed to be), meaning that it is valid to ask for and receive 5 things, for example, if an entity has, say, 3 overrides and there are 3 other nodes in the ring.\r\n\r\nThis PR fixes a couple related issues in mishandling these situations:\r\n- We would stop searching the ring if the number of found overrides + found entries in ring == size of the ring, even if we still needed more entries\r\n- We would never stop searching if the number of overrides was more than the size of the ring but less than the number of entries requested",
        "reactions": {
          "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/discord/ex_hash_ring/issues/13/reactions",
